        FILED by agent(review-3069) out of four-failures-newly-visible-after-gate-manifest-stopped-aborting-the-run,
        so it does not disappear when that aggregate closes. This is the ONE genuine
        product signal from the 2026-09-17 validate run; everything else that run
        produced was an instrument defect or a bar raise.
        
        THE CELL
          test:     c-programs/setitimer-determinism
          mode:     verify
          backend:  kvm          (lane portable, category c-programs)
          node:     e2e.manifest_c_programs
        
        WHAT DIVERGES
        The guest calls setitimer, which raises SIGALRM. Instead of being delivered to
        the guest under determinism control, THE SIGNAL KILLS THE SANDBOX CONTAINER:
        
          :: Run1...
          HERMIT_INTERNAL_FAILURE class=container-child-exit status=Signaled(SIGALRM, false)
          Error: Sandbox container exited unexpectedly: Signaled(SIGALRM, false)
        
        The run therefore never reaches a comparison:
          verdict=no_result, no_result_reason={kind: not_run},
          infrastructure_error=null, comparison=null
        
        THE DISCRIMINATOR THAT MAKES IT PRODUCT RATHER THAN ENVIRONMENT
        The IDENTICAL cell PASSES on ptrace in the same run. It is backend-specific, so
        the test is not wrong and the host is not at fault. Consistent with the standing
        observation that reverie-kvm has no signal delivery, so KVM greens certify
        installation and never delivery.
        
        SHAS -- MEASURED, NOT TAKEN FROM A LEDGER RECORD
          REPRODUCED AT BASE:  79da523137
              Built FROM SOURCE and run WITHOUT --prebuilt, which also rules out stale
              prepared artifacts. Signature byte-identical to the validate run's.
              Command:
                ./target/debug/test-harness run --lane portable \
                  --category c-programs --test c-programs/setitimer-determinism \
                  --mode verify --backend kvm
          OBSERVED IN THE VALIDATE RUN AT:  2959c577741bea5312832a6abdf653abbf9c760c
              unit validate-pr3080-2959c577-review3069, node e2e.manifest_c_programs,
              129s, exit 1.
          STILL PRESENT AT:  1bc8d15c975c989bee700f0253e32ec7ecde991b (PR 3080 head)
              Nothing on that branch touches runtime code -- the only files it changes
              are scripts/validate.rs, ci/manifest-plan/src/validation_dag_static.rs and
              the generated ci/dag/validate.json.
        
        IT IS A REGRESSION, AND I CHECKED THAT PROPERLY RATHER THAN ASSUMING
        A green in cells.json says WHEN a cell last passed, never WHICH CHECK it passed,
        so "it was green" is not sufficient. The two questions that are:
          1. Was the same check in force? YES -- the verify mechanism dates to
             2026-08-16 (9e88341c28), long before the recorded green.
          2. Was the cell enabled then? YES -- at c7520a6c3873 the kvm/verify entry
             reads enabled=True status=green (chaos and replay are not-applicable).
        Contrast the five backend-parity-c cells in the same run, which FAIL both tests
        and are a bar raise rather than a regression.
        
        BISECT BOUND, with the caveat it needs
          c7520a6c3873 (2026-09-10 15:31), ~305 commits back from the run head.
          ⚠️ This comes from last_tested in the record, which is exactly the kind of
          value shown unreliable tonight -- one sibling record named 26bda94103ad, which
          is NOT an ancestor of HEAD at all and points at rebased-away history. I
          VERIFIED this one: git merge-base --is-ancestor c7520a6c3873 HEAD succeeds, so
          it is a usable lower bound. Re-verify before relying on it.
          Worth looking at first inside that window: de6a9910e "Align KVM validation
          selections with measured inventories", which gave the KVM lane the
          kvm-execution-tests feature and moved several KVM counts. NOT established as
          the cause -- named only as the most plausible starting point.
        
        SECONDARY DEFECT, SEPARABLE AND ARGUABLY WORSE
        The crash is recorded as verdict=no_result with reason kind=not_run and
        infrastructure_error=null. THE CONTAINER RAN AND DIED. Filing a fatal signal as
        "not_run" puts a real product defect in the never-measured bucket rather than
        the product-failure one, so it is invisible in the place people look for reds.
        Fixing the signal delivery without fixing this classification leaves the next
        such crash equally silent.
